# {{project.name}}

Bare-metal RISC-V firmware for QEMU's `virt` machine.

```bash
mcpp build                            # firmware + .bin + .map + a size summary
mcpp run                              # boots in qemu
mcpp test                             # each tests/*.cpp runs as its own image
mcpp build --target riscv32-none-elf  # the other width, same source
```

The board — libc, startup, memory layout and the emulator — comes from
[`{{template.package.name}}`](https://github.com/{{template.package.namespace}}/{{template.package.name}}),
declared in `mcpp.toml` as an ordinary dependency. Changing boards is changing
that line.

## What to look at first

| | |
|---|---|
| `src/main.cpp` | an ordinary `int main()` — the board package supplies the crt0 that calls it |
| `tests/boots.cpp` | a test that runs **on the target**, under the emulator |
| `mcpp.toml` | `[build] target` picks the ISA; there is no `[target.*]` section |

The `.map` beside the built ELF is where to look when a section did not end up
where expected, and the size summary printed after each build is the number
that decides whether the image fits.
